From 7eb5b41fa9813191fb0970434e875e5be88bd714 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:21:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 158/274] Kernel preparation: routing, activation, norm,
 Engram, collective and L2-prefetch kernels declare from configuration

The gate router declares route_partials for each (image, routing mask) a decode
step can pass and binds them into its kernel table; it warms TileKernels' top-k
gate when a forward can route more rows than the gate's split rows (the drafter
bounds its rows by its query blocks). The routing mask variants follow
VLLM_MOE_SKIP_PADDING and the model runner. Decoder layers declare their
router, which is not a module.

TileLangRMSNorm warms TileKernels' norm of its width; the shared expert's
activation declares the kernel of its owner's width. Engram declares its packed
gate, and the blocked gate when prefill sequence parallelism runs with a
column-parallel projection; a disk table declares its row kernels and the hash
state its hash. The model declares the rank-order sum of the TP group's
collectives and the TileLang L2 prefetch, now a JIT factory keyed by its grid,
block and chunk.

